","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"For resentment kills a fool, and envy slays the simple.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":29,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"When the Lordsaw that Leah was unloved, He opened her womb; but Rachel was barren.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And his brothers were jealous of him, but his father kept in mind what he had said.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For He has looked with favor on the humble state of His servant. From now on all generations will call me blessed.","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":16,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Sarai said to Abram, “Look now, the Lordhas prevented me from bearing children. Please go to my maidservant; perhaps I can build a family by her.” And Abram listened to the voice of Sarai.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Gad will be attacked by raiders, but he will attack their heels.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He saw Ephraimʼs sons to the third generation, and indeed the sons of Machir son of Manasseh were brought up on Josephʼs knees.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":35,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Vindicate me by Your righteousness, O LORD my God, and do not let them gloat over me.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":9}]},"14-24":{"people":[{"id":"leah-h3812","name":"Leah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Rachel","count":6,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":3,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"issachar-h3485g","name":"Issachar","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"zebulun-h2074","name":"Zebulun","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"dinah-h1783","name":"Dinah","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's daughter","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3812","lemma":"לֵאָה","tr":"le·ah","gloss":"Leah","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":34},{"base":"H1736","lemma":"דּוּדַי","tr":"du·day","gloss":"mandrake","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":6},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":496},{"base":"H2029","lemma":"הָרָה","tr":"ha·rah","gloss":"to conceive","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":43},{"base":"H7354","lemma":"רָחֵל","tr":"ra·chel","gloss":"Rachel","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":47},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":733},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":864},{"base":"H7936","lemma":"סָכַר","tr":"sa·khar","gloss":"to hire","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":21},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":350},{"base":"H7901","lemma":"שָׁכַב","tr":"sha·khav","gloss":"to lie down: lay down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":212}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":29,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"When the Lordsaw that Leah was unloved, He opened her womb; but Rachel was barren.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":8,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"But God remembered Noah and all the animals and livestock that were with him in the ark. And God sent a wind over the earth, and the waters began to subside.","from":22},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"“The Lord has done this for me. In these days He has shown me favor and taken away my disgrace among the people.”","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":113,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"He settles the barren woman in her home as a joyful mother to her children. Hallelujah!","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now the Lordattended to Sarah as He had said, and the Lorddid for Sarah what He had promised.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So Sarah conceived and bore a son to Abraham in his old age, at the very time God had promised.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Later, Isaac prayed to the Lordon behalf of his wife, because she was barren. And the Lordheard his prayer, and his wife Rebekah conceived.","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The next morning they got up early to bow in worship before the LORD, and then they returned home to Ramah. And Elkanah had relations with his wife Hannah, and the LORD remembered her.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":8}]},"25-36":{"people":[{"id":"laban-h3837a","name":"Laban","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bethuel","count":4,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2921","lemma":"טָלָא","tr":"ta·la","gloss":"to spot","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":8},{"base":"H5348","lemma":"נָקֹד","tr":"na·qod","gloss":"speckled","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":9},{"base":"H2345","lemma":"חוּם","tr":"chum","gloss":"darkened","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":4},{"base":"H3837","lemma":"לָבָן","tr":"la·van","gloss":"Laban","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":55},{"base":"H3775","lemma":"כֶּ֫שֶׂב","tr":"ke·sev","gloss":"sheep","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":13},{"base":"H7939","lemma":"שָׂכָר","tr":"sa·khar","gloss":"wages","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":28},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":350},{"base":"H5795","lemma":"עֵז","tr":"ez","gloss":"goat","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":74},{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":274},{"base":"H5647","lemma":"עָבַד","tr":"a·vad","gloss":"to serve","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":288}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":2,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"“My lord,” she said, “may I continue to find favor in your eyes, for you have comforted and spoken kindly to your maidservant, though I am not like one of your servant girls.”","from":27},{"book":"ISA","chapter":61,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Their descendants will be known among the nations, and their offspring among the peoples. All who see them will acknowledge that they are a people the LORD has blessed.","from":27},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"and rescued him from all his troubles. He granted Joseph favor and wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king of Egypt, who appointed him ruler over Egypt and all his household.","from":27},{"book":"1TI","chapter":5,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"If anyone does not provide for his own, and especially his own household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever.","from":30},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"and that night the Lordappeared to him and said, “I am the God of your father Abraham. Do not be afraid, for I am with you. I will bless you and multiply your descendants for the sake of My servant Abraham.”","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"I will bless those who bless you and curse those who curse you; and all the families of the earth will be blessed through you.”","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":39,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"the Lordwas with him and extended kindness to him, granting him favor in the eyes of the prison warden.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":39,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The warden did not concern himself with anything under Josephʼs care, because the Lordwas with Joseph and gave him success in whatever he did.","from":27}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"37-43":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"laban-h3837a","name":"Laban","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bethuel","count":2,"firstVerse":40}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":11,"uses":274},{"base":"H4731","lemma":"מַקֵּל","tr":"maq·qel","gloss":"rod","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":18},{"base":"H3179","lemma":"יָחַם","tr":"ya·cham","gloss":"to conceive","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":6},{"base":"H3837","lemma":"לָבָן","tr":"la·van","gloss":"Laban","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":55},{"base":"H6478","lemma":"פָּצַל","tr":"pa·tsal","gloss":"to peel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":350},{"base":"H7298","lemma":"רַ֫הַט","tr":"ra·hat","gloss":"trough","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H6124","lemma":"עָקֹד","tr":"a·qod","gloss":"striped","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H5848","lemma":"עָטַף","tr":"a·taph","gloss":"to turn aside","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H3836","lemma":"לָבָן","tr":"la·van","gloss":"white","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":29}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“The Lordhas greatly blessed my master, and he has become rich. He has given him sheep and cattle, silver and gold, menservants and maidservants, camels and donkeys.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"and he became richer and richer, until he was exceedingly wealthy.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"He owned so many flocks and herds and servants that the Philistines envied him.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Indeed, you had very little before my arrival, but now your wealth has increased many times over. The Lordhas blessed you wherever I set foot. But now, when may I also provide for my own household?”","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Abram had become extremely wealthy in livestock and silver and gold.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":13,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he became richer and richer, until he was exceedingly wealthy. He owned so many flocks and herds and servants that the Philistines envied him.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Look, I am with you, and I will watch over you wherever you go, and I will bring you back to this land. For I will not leave you until I have done what I have promised you.”","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":7,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And although he has cheated me and changed my wages ten times, God has not allowed him to harm me. If he said, ‘The speckled will be your wages,’ then the whole flock bore speckled offspring. If he said, ‘The streaked will be your wages,’ then the whole flock bore streaked offspring.","from":43}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}